    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "GPT-5.6 Sol on darwin1859-ch06-06: partially-resolvable, resolvability 0.74";
    dc:description "Current behaviour and retained anatomy can be documented directly in many species. Existing data support the existence claim, but historical precedence usually requires uncertain ancestral reconstruction.";
    dc:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/dataset-resolvability-0.1.0>;
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment> "Proposed test with existing data: Identify species whose observed habitat use or behaviour differs from that predicted by homologous structures and close relatives, then reconstruct whether behavioural shifts precede structural evolution. Repeated behavioural mismatch with retained ancestral anatomy supports the claim.";
    prov:wasAttributedTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/agent/delphisci-resolvability-assessor-gpt-5.6-sol-medium>;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/assessmentType> "dataset-resolvability/0.1.0";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/evidenceAgainst> "Present-day mismatch does not by itself establish the temporal order of habit and structural change.", "Structure-function mismatch requires an explicit expectation model.";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasConfidence> "0.81"^^xsd:double;
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hasEvidence> <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-06--gpt--dataset-1>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-06--gpt--dataset-2>, <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/darwin1859-ch06-06--gpt--dataset-3>;
